# The measure

## What is re-derived here

The fix claims one thing about a child's spend: a continuation is a **new session**, so the rule that answers a
re-read inside one session cannot answer it, and the rule that does — the item's ledger rule — is what the new bullet
states. Both halves are re-derived below through the tools both entry points share; the ledger the bullet names is
read from a real item and not from this change's own runs.

## The real ledger's shape

Read-only, from the main tree (`.pi/issue-loop/items/1030/`, the item the issue names as the one whose continuation was
running when it was filed): five tab-separated columns and no header row, `sha`, turn, size, session, path.

$ head -1 /home/tim/projects/NaviVeylin/.pi/issue-loop/items/1030/tool-result-ledger.tsv
96a34944b919076fbbbffc322d50bfee	1	16479	worker-prompt	worker-prompt.md

$ sed -n '2p' /home/tim/projects/NaviVeylin/.pi/issue-loop/items/1030/tool-result-ledger.tsv
1ffd448a18bac55adfd09331e84fb601	17	3023	reviewer-prompt-2	work-package.md

The session column is the name of the prompt file the reading child was given, and the ledger is the item's: 70 lines
over that item, the worker phase's 3 and its continuation's 39 in the **same file** —

$ cut -f4 …/items/1030/tool-result-ledger.tsv | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn
     39 worker-prompt-continuation
      9 reviewer-prompt-2
      8 worker-tail-round2-prompt
      5 worker-prompt-round2
      3 worker-tail-prompt
      3 worker-prompt
      2 reviewer-prompt-1-restart
      1 reviewer-prompt-1

— while the two processes' **reports** are two files, each written once:

$ ls -l …/items/1030/worker-report.md …/items/1030/worker-continuation-report.md
-rw-r--r-- 1 tim tim 3609 25. Nov 06:27 …/items/1030/worker-continuation-report.md
-rw-r--r-- 1 tim tim 1174 25. Nov 06:09 …/items/1030/worker-report.md

So an item split at its checkpoint holds one ledger of both sessions and two reports, the second process's being
`worker-continuation-report.md` (`run.sh:1292`, `run_child "$item_dir/worker-prompt-continuation.md"
"$item_dir/worker-continuation-report.md"`) — which is why the bullet points at `worker-report.md` as well as at the
ledger: the ledger says what was read, and only that file says what was made of it.

## The rule the bullet states, re-derived

`tools/pi-trim-result.mjs`'s CLI applies `repeatResult` — the item-ledger rule — because the ledger is the one the CLI
is handed (`--ledger`); its own comment says why the other rule cannot appear there: "One invocation is one child that
reads one path once, so the repeat-read tally is always empty here". That is the correction the bullet carries: the
per-child tally (`repeatReadResult`, `read.child`, issues #925 and #989) is a `Map` that lives as long as one child
process, so a continuation starts with it empty and no path of its first process can be in it; the item ledger
(`read.ledger`, `LOOP_TOOL_RESULT_LEDGER`, issue #685) is the file every child of the item opens.

One path, three reads, one ledger — each invocation is one session:

$ node tools/pi-trim-result.mjs --bound 120000 --tool read --path notes.md --turn 1 --session worker-prompt \
    --ledger "$d/ledger.tsv" < "$d/notes.md"          # the first process reads it, 18 characters
line one
line two
exit 0

$ cat "$d/ledger.tsv"
e9024f1a07d29d52ad3aa5e1a18e94db	1	18	worker-prompt	notes.md

$ node tools/pi-trim-result.mjs --bound 120000 --tool read --path notes.md --turn 2 --session worker-prompt-continuation \
    --ledger "$d/ledger.tsv" < "$d/notes.md"          # the continuation, a new session, reads the same path unchanged
[LOOP-ALREADY-READ: notes.md (18 characters) was read at turn 1 in the worker-prompt session and is unchanged since — read a range instead of the whole file again (ctx_read mode="lines:N-M")]
exit 0

$ node tools/pi-trim-result.mjs --bound 120000 --tool read --path big.md --turn 2 --session worker-prompt-continuation \
    --ledger "$d/ledger.tsv" < "$d/big.md"             # 6 010 characters, changed since turn 1
… (the first 2 000 characters)
[LOOP-REPEAT-EDIT: big.md changed since turn 1; the first 2000 of 6010 characters are shown — read the rest in ranges (ctx_read mode="lines:N-M")]
exit 0

Read: a path the item already holds is answered across the session boundary with the one line the bullet promises —
the turn, the size, the session that read it and the range call — and a path that changed since with a bounded head and
the `[LOOP-REPEAT-EDIT: …]` line. The bullet's two arms are the two the rule has, in the order it states them.

## What the change adds to the prompt

The skeleton the issue measured at 4 665 B (`tools/loop/prompts/worker-continuation.md` at `adb79f6f`) is 5 735 B after
the change (+1 070): one bullet naming the ledger, its columns, the rule over it and the report beside it, and the
sentence that the first process's own notes still stand in the scratch directory — spent once per continuation, against
the 6.63 Mtok a worker session costs and the 11.34 Mtok a `worker-rework` item costs.
